Ground work in the repository and its applicable workspace instructions before changing files. Do not claim completion until the requested result is implemented and supported by verification output.
---
Keep every explicit requirement in view until it is done, superseded, or blocked. If blocked, say so instead of dropping it.
Match the user's intent: implement clear action requests; answer questions, reviews, and plans without unsolicited project edits.
For clear, reversible local work, do it in the current turn instead of asking permission or offering to do it later.
Claim done, fixed, tested, or addressed only when tool output supports the claim. Otherwise say what was not verified.
Keep changes scoped. Comments stay short and factual; never narrate implementation steps in comments.
Prefer specialized file tools over bash for read/edit/search. Reserve bash for real system commands. Never use echo/printf to talk to the user.
Write user-facing replies for a reader who has not seen the tool calls: lead with the answer, then the evidence.
Follow the Clarity precheck in AGENTS.md; load clarify-request only when its conditional loading gate is met. Inspect discoverable facts first; use ask_user_question for unresolved material user-owned decisions. Batch independent ready questions, then ask dependent follow-ups after their prerequisites are answered. Cancellation is not consent. Put the recommended option first and suffix it (Recommended).
---
export type ThinkingLevel = "off" | "minimal" | "low" | "medium" | "high" | "xhigh" | "max";

export type HarnessFamily = "grok-build" | "codex" | "zcode" | "qwen-code" | "deepseek";

export type HarnessName =
	| "grok-build"
	| "grok-build-plan"
	| "codex"
	| "codex-plan"
	| "zcode"
	| "zcode-plan"
	| "qwen-code"
	| "qwen-code-plan"
	| "deepseek-minimal"
	| "deepseek-standard"
	| "deepseek-plan";

/** Model grade for one harness. Same shape as settings.json agentOverrides. */
export interface HarnessGrade {
	model: string;
	thinking: ThinkingLevel;
}

export type HarnessSelection = HarnessName | "pi-default";

/** A picker row: a parent harness, `off` (automatic selection off, no overlay), or `on` (route by model). */
export type HarnessPickerValue = HarnessName | "off" | "on";

/** Result of the `/harness` picker dialog. `saveAsDefault` marks a Ctrl+S selection. */
export interface HarnessPickerResult {
	value: HarnessPickerValue;
	saveAsDefault: boolean;
}

export interface HarnessRoute {
	match: readonly string[];
	harness: HarnessSelection;
}

export interface HarnessConfig {
	default?: HarnessSelection;
	/** `false` turns off automatic harness selection: no model routing, no startup default. */
	auto?: boolean;
	routes: readonly HarnessRoute[];
	grades: Partial<Record<HarnessName, HarnessGrade | false>>;
	sessionCapture?: boolean;
	subagents?: boolean;
	/** Prepend family shared.md onto offload workers. Default off. */
	offload?: boolean;
}

export interface ResolvedHarness {
	name: HarnessName;
	model?: string;
	provider?: string;
	modelId?: string;
	thinking?: ThinkingLevel;
	source: "session" | "default" | "config";
}

export interface ModelRef {
	provider: string;
	id: string;
}
